config AMNEZIAWG
	tristate "AmneziaWG secure network tunnel"
	depends on NET && INET
	depends on IPV6 || !IPV6
	select NET_UDP_TUNNEL
	select DST_CACHE
	select CRYPTO
	select CRYPTO_ALGAPI
	select ARM_CRYPTO if ARM
	select ARM64_CRYPTO if ARM64
	select VFP
	select VFPv3 if CPU_V7
	select NEON if CPU_V7
	select KERNEL_MODE_NEON if CPU_V7
	help
	  AmneziaWG is WireGuard with traffic obfuscation: junk packets before
	  the handshake, random prefixes and configurable message types, so
	  that the tunnel cannot be recognised by its packet signatures. With
	  all obfuscation parameters left at zero it speaks plain WireGuard.

	  It uses its own generic netlink family ("amneziawg") and its own
	  link kind ("amneziawg"), so it can be built together with WIREGUARD.
	  It is configured with the awg tool from amneziawg-tools.

	  It's safe to say Y or M here, as the driver is very lightweight and
	  is only in use when an administrator chooses to add an interface.

config AMNEZIAWG_DEBUG
	bool "Debugging checks and verbose messages"
	depends on AMNEZIAWG
	help
	  This will write log messages for handshake and other events
	  that occur for an AmneziaWG interface. It will also perform some
	  extra validation checks and unit tests at various points. This is
	  only useful for debugging.

	  Say N here unless you know what you're doing.
